{"id": "clm:8ff33caa2775f002165de58c84012c3df45b4705d44e468b346d928a1871a1dc", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB's covered-query requirements say a single index must contain every query field, fields needed internally for sharding, and every returned field; on mongos, the index must contain the shard key. A general compound-index guide also notes that _id must be indexed or excluded from the projection. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/query-optimization/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hashed and compound hashed shard keys and index coverage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/OneUptime/blog/blob/master/posts/2026-01-30-mongodb-compound-index-strategies/README.md", "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76295889/mongodb-index-need-to-include-id-for-it-to-cover-if-projecting-id"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0cafab12e00ffd59b1acc6dfa606778d9d4f184f65f7c55a00fdfeedc5750fff", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7e0cdcb2464dedf4226003c259b4c840a5bee4c0ca855df7f38cd98ace184aed", "ev:9b3faac145e939253fb3a6991f3a98ee334ee7d1e2c27e405f03fa089557281c", "ev:d9123880f460445c4d440b772c90366b8243305a988570d7288a7c80631cc943"]}
{"id": "clm:87111bf9768b6515ebcc8223795d3b40ca12502777e407867c1ea6c971ca98b3", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB's hashed-index manual says hashed indexes cannot cover a query. Its server test shows that find({_id: true}, {_id: 0}) against a collection sharded by {_id: \"hashed\"} still has totalDocsExamined: 1, so the hashed shard-key value is not returned from the index alone. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-20)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hashed and compound hashed shard keys and index coverage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/jstests/sharding/covered_shard_key_indexes.js", "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/jstests/sharding/covered_shard_key_indexes.js"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0cafab12e00ffd59b1acc6dfa606778d9d4f184f65f7c55a00fdfeedc5750fff", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:327915c8e9b7766a2b6069835ba63cdb6f1fa51b7954351ec057067924be7483", "ev:6b7342859339aba7d27f397e078a18b375fab5eb1c4dbddd4079aff2f0050cc6"]}
{"id": "clm:38975f54c5df3935fbf266044ef01f0ac4f2641a8bc4f0e5fe6ade7406566fd2", "type": "statement", "text": "With a single-field hashed shard key, equality matches can target one shard; hashing preserves distribution for monotonically changing values but removes original-value range locality, so a range predicate cannot use the hashed index and may broadcast to multiple shards. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-08-04)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/hashed-sharding/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hashed and compound hashed shard keys and index coverage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed/create.md", "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/configure-sharding-to-maximize-the-performance-of-shards"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0cafab12e00ffd59b1acc6dfa606778d9d4f184f65f7c55a00fdfeedc5750fff", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9bfde41286febc780bacf7ec56991f95fee063377a2bd2f1c38e4c1a1ef1307e", "ev:ca9e1f2ba635d11062778e9f2ddd0a6e295e96ded718a5dce607590369ef76b9", "ev:f8448248bd1769132e8d4d048d4ba6d52683a7a2d22e10c9744fe6cdc430658a"]}
{"id": "clm:56f185f5d1e8d75a2d1e16e9c6ac3d85d36ff9ffdc04dfabe53a1401173aef55", "type": "statement", "text": "Inference for compound hashed shard keys: MongoDB defines the compound form as an index with one hashed key and other ordinary ordered keys, while its index-type manual says hashed indexes cannot cover queries. The compound hashed index should therefore be treated as non-covering even when ordinary fields match the query and projection. The cited server test directly checks only a single-field hashed shard key, not this compound case. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-20)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hashed and compound hashed shard keys and index coverage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed/create.md", "https://www.percona.com/blog/refining-shard-keys-in-mongodb-4-4-and-above/", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/jstests/sharding/covered_shard_key_indexes.js"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0cafab12e00ffd59b1acc6dfa606778d9d4f184f65f7c55a00fdfeedc5750fff", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:327915c8e9b7766a2b6069835ba63cdb6f1fa51b7954351ec057067924be7483", "ev:9b230d5de6d6e65e8928c7d56ff14a27dfe10c96e0a7536c3c00fe6b2cee9145", "ev:abe1946373b8c980ef417f962402c0c2394729f231c9a81b0cc2db8b8c8463ac"]}
{"id": "clm:549025cae6545da6c78858de1250ad4c1029019170f5f4ee69273bf297f59f7b", "type": "statement", "text": "A compound hashed index hashes one field only and stores its other fields with ascending or descending order; the hashed field can be combined with ordinary fields before or after it. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed/create.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hashed and compound hashed shard keys and index coverage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/sharding-with-zones-based-on-compound-shard-keys-on-mongodb-4-4/", "https://www.percona.com/blog/refining-shard-keys-in-mongodb-4-4-and-above/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0cafab12e00ffd59b1acc6dfa606778d9d4f184f65f7c55a00fdfeedc5750fff", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5084d273dd5adb2d1ea0e7acddcc85d51def8a7ed3c1b5ecda006c74962b85ca", "ev:9b230d5de6d6e65e8928c7d56ff14a27dfe10c96e0a7536c3c00fe6b2cee9145"]}
{"id": "clm:bed8b1959496e594258c77aa7410dd68341723f428b966698a51b8e45c08558e", "type": "statement", "text": "A non-hashed prefix in a compound hashed shard key can define zone ranges while the hashed field distributes values more evenly; this combination does not make the compound hashed index cover queries. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/hashed-sharding/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hashed and compound hashed shard keys and index coverage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/sharding-with-zones-based-on-compound-shard-keys-on-mongodb-4-4/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0cafab12e00ffd59b1acc6dfa606778d9d4f184f65f7c55a00fdfeedc5750fff", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:327915c8e9b7766a2b6069835ba63cdb6f1fa51b7954351ec057067924be7483", "ev:9b5bde6b7ee8a4873125d8a78e5dbab58048db3c4f9abe05e04114610c9775b3"]}
